{
  "slug": "sfdx-iq",
  "name": "Sfdx Iq",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "This plugin gives Claude Code deep Salesforce expertise. When you install it, Claude understands Salesforce best practices -- security, governor limits, permission models, flows, deployments -- and applies them automatically to everything it builds or reviews for you.\n\nAsk Claude to review your Apex code, design a data model, check your flows, build a trigger, or plan a feature -- and it will follow Salesforce platform rules without you having to remind it.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **7 agents** and **21 commands**.\n\n- **Agents** (7): `apex-code-reviewer` (Use this agent to review Apex code (classes, triggers, batch, queueable, schedulable) for best practices, governor limit risks,…), `devops-coordinator` (Use this agent for Salesforce DevOps tasks including deployment strategy, test patterns (TDD, TestDataFactory, mocks), org health analysis,…), `flow-analyst` (Use this agent to analyze Salesforce Flows for best practices including DML optimization, fault path coverage, before-save vs…), `integration-specialist` (Use this agent for Salesforce integration patterns including Named Credentials, REST/SOAP callouts, Platform Events, Change Data Capture, async…), `lwc-reviewer` (Use this agent to review Lightning Web Components for best practices including proper decorator usage, lifecycle hooks, event…), `security-auditor` (Use this agent to review Salesforce code and configuration for security vulnerabilities including CRUD/FLS enforcement, sharing model compliance,…), `solution-designer` (Use this agent for Salesforce solution architecture and implementation planning)\n- **Commands** (21): `apex-class` (Create, review, refine, or debug Apex classes (service, selector, controller, utility, domain)), `apex-test` (Create or improve Apex test classes with coverage targeting and Salesforce best practices), `async-apex` (Create, refine, or debug async Apex (Batch, Queueable, Schedulable, Future methods)), `code-review` (Full code review across Apex, LWC, and Flows using specialized agents), `csiq-help` (Show available sfdx-iq commands and usage help), `data-model` (Analyze or design Salesforce data model with relationship mapping), `debug-log` (Retrieve and analyze Salesforce debug logs), `doctor` (Diagnose environment configuration for Salesforce development (alternative to npx sfdx-iq doctor)), and 13 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install sfdx-iq@claude-community` from `bhanu91221/sfdx-iq`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "agent": 7,
    "command": 21
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
